course: dictionary
lesson: 11719
title: Authorisation: who is allowed?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Authorisation is official permission to do something. When someone has authorisation, they have been allowed to do it, usually by a person in charge. «Only staff with authorisation may enter the lab.» The clues are only and may: most people are not allowed in, but staff have been given permission.
explain: Authorisation is a noun, and it comes from the verb authorise, which means to give permission. Context helps you spot the meaning: «Mum gave written authorisation for the school trip.» Written suggests a signed note or form, and gave tells you permission was handed over.
explain: Sometimes authorisation is a code rather than a note. «Type your authorisation code to approve the payment.» Ask yourself what would fit: permission or code both make sense here, so the word is about being allowed. Then swap in your meaning to check: «Type your permission to approve the payment» sounds a little odd, but the idea still works.
fact: Authorisation means official permission to do something.
fact: An authorisation can also be a document or a code that gives that permission.
fact: «Without authorisation» means without being allowed: «You cannot leave the building without authorisation.»
fact: Phrases to know: give authorisation, written authorisation, authorisation code.
fact: In American English the spelling is authorization, with a z, but the meaning is the same.
exercise: «Only staff with authorisation may enter the room.» What does authorisation mean here? | A type of door | *Official permission to go in | A map of the building | A loud warning bell
exercise: «Sam could not go on the trip without written authorisation from home.» What did Sam need? | A bus ticket | *A signed note giving permission | A packed lunch | A new coat
exercise: What is an authorisation code? | A code for a secret message in a film | A score from a sports match | A list of school rules | *A special code that shows you are allowed to do something
test: What does «without authorisation» mean? | With a heavy bag | With a big smile | Very quickly | *Without permission
test: Which word is closest in meaning to authorisation? | *Permission | Confusion | Holiday | Mistake
exam: Mum's note says «I give my authorisation for Ella to use the library computer.» What does this mean? | Ella has broken the computer | Ella is the librarian | Mum has lost her note | *Ella has been given permission to use the computer
